 the most efficient play.\n\nReason: You should play the ♠10 to beat the ♥5. The 10 is your lowest isolated single card. By playing it, you maintain the integrity of your powerful combinations (Triple 4s, Triple Qs, Pair of Aces, Pair of 2s) and high control cards (King, Black Joker). This move cleans up your hand structure, leaving you with two potential Full Houses (e.g., 444+AA and QQQ+22) or Triplet-based plays, along with high cards to regain initiative. Playing a higher card like the King would be wasteful, and breaking the Queens would weaken your hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠10"]}'}
