ce out the Red Joker, which would make my pair of 2s the highest remaining cards.\n\nReason: The opponent played a 2, a very high card. I have the Black Joker, which is the only card that can beat it. Since my hand relies on Full Houses (444AA, QQQ22) and I have very few singles, I cannot afford to pass and let the opponents continue leading singles. Gaining the lead allows me to dictate the pattern (Full Houses), or at minimum, forces the Red Joker out, empowering my pair of 2s for late-game control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["BlackJoker"]}'}
